# Testing Hermeticity

Unit tests must be deterministic and independent of developer machines.

- Never depend on:
  - live network services
  - external APIs
  - developer home directories
  - local credentials
  - ambient environment state

- Mock external dependencies including:
  - HTTP requests
  - LLM calls
  - databases
  - filesystem-backed stores
  - cloud services

- Tests must pass identically with credentials present and absent.

- Use temporary directories and isolated fixtures instead of real user data.

- Before submitting changes, run:
  - type checks
  - unit tests
  - builds
  - packaging checks
  - smoke tests
